Here's a ``diff'' script for /usr/src/usr.bin/file.c on 4.2BSD, which
will produce a version of file which will recognize some additional
file types. You may not wish to include all these changes, since some
of the file types are local to the machines at U of M. The part which
recognizes compacted files by unpacking the first block and then
identiying that is cute, but slow sometimes.

The additional types it recognizes are: Simpl source code, Z80 object
code, PDP-11 object code, Pyramid object code, CVL format pictures,
compacted files, exec-able scripts and tar archives.

